- Story & Context: Bassist Freja wrote the chord progression on a cracked tape machine after spending three days locked in the mall's abandoned record shop listening to Stan Getz and solar flare telemetry recordings. Her brother brought his flugelhorn into the empty escalators, using the seven-second concrete echo to harmonize with his own breathing. During the final take, an old arcade speaker blew out with a dry pop, leaving only the pristine, woody thrum of the nylon strings echoing into the rafters. "Hold your breath or the tape will catch the frost," she whispered into the ribbon mic before the final chord resolved.
