Track 3: Kjøpesenter Orbit
- Story & Context: On the final night before municipal bulldozers reclaimed the ghost mall, the quartet set up on the roof under a blinding Aurora Borealis. They jammed a single modal chord for twenty-two minutes while local teenagers ran audio cables down three flights of stairs to broadcast the track over the town's pirate FM frequency. When the police finally cut the generator, the tail end of Astrid's acoustic strum was still ringing inside every car radio parked within five miles. "The sky is just an empty room waiting for a horn," a voice recorded on the opening tape loop endlessly repeats.
